description: Record durable technical decisions as the project evolves
alwaysApply: true
---

# Decision Records

- Record decisions that affect architecture, dependencies, data ownership, security posture, deployment, or future agent behavior.
- Use lightweight decision records: context, decision, consequences, and date are enough.
- Prefer one durable decision record over scattering the same rationale across comments, chat summaries, and ad hoc notes.
- Update or supersede old decisions when reality changes. Do not leave conflicting guidance unaddressed.
- If a decision is still tentative, label it as tentative and state what would make it final.
